WEBVTT

1  
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740  
My first sock here is my sclera.  
  
2  
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:08.540  
The second layer is the uvea, made up of the choroid, the iris, and the  
  
3  
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.660  
ciliary body.  
  
4  
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.020  
I remove that, and then I am left with the retina,  
  
5  
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.280  
which consists primarily of two main layers,  
  
6  
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.260  
the outer retina and the inner retina.  
  
7  
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.660  
This is where the detachment occurs, where we have the moment of the primitive optic cup  
  
8  
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.000  
coming in like this, making the right connection.  
  
9  
00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:30.077  
with the epiblast  
  
10  
00:00:30.077 --> 00:00:31.877  
of the surface that will  
  
11  
00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:33.897  
thicken, creating the  
  
12  
00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:35.757  
outer optic placode, which is  
  
13  
00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.737  
held here, growing around it.  
  
14  
00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:39.757  
This creates the primitive depression.  
  
15  
00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:41.317  
Then it will  
  
16  
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:43.457  
be integrated like this.  
  
17  
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:45.437  
We have the meeting  
  
18  
00:00:45.437 --> 00:00:47.797  
of this retina wrapping around  
  
19  
00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:49.857  
and this is where it will create what we call  
  
20  
00:00:49.857 --> 00:00:52.117  
the outer retina and the retina  
  
21  
00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:54.217  
interior. This is where you have the detachment  
  
22  
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.057  
of the retina. There are people who have a detachment.  
  
23  
00:01:00.854  
of the retina. You've probably heard of that. This is where it actually happens. And the retina,  
  
24  
00:01:00.954 --> 00:01:05.294  
if you look at it, is really brain, ventricular tissue.